<title>SPAIN: Dutch premier praises Spain economic progress.</title>
<headline>Dutch premier praises Spain economic progress.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch Prime Minister Wim Kok on Monday praised Spain's economic progress in the past year.</p>
<p>Speaking to a conference in Madrid, Kok stressed the importance of including as many countries as possible in the launch of a single European currency set for 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;Allow me to add in this connection how encouraged and impressed I am by the Spanish economic and budgetary achievements of the last year,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>Kok, whose country holds the presidency of the European Union, was on a tour of Portugal, Spain and Italy to discuss a European summit in Amsterdam planned for June.</p>
</text>
